module fn_type_param.neg_1

// NOVAC_EXPECT a parameter of function type
// ONE seeded cause: a COMPILED declaration whose parameter is typed by a
// function type (D43). The signature READS since 2026-10-31 (task 134,
// class A2) -- that is what keeps a handed declaration like std's
// `map_err` in the registry instead of dropping it into "no such method" --
// but no VALUE of a function type is compiled while closure literals are
// refused, so a compiled declaration with one is refused by name rather
// than emitted into an ice on the C layout. The body never calls the
// parameter, so the refusal at the declaration stays the ONLY cause.
fn apply(f fn(int) -> int, x int) -> int => x

fn main() {
    println(1)
}
